      {
        "review_id": 350573032,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r350573032-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Utterly Fascinating. Sensory overload, great historical and social experience",
        "text": "I must say that I had no idea what I was about to see, I just had a couple of days in Kathmandu before an Everest Base Camp Trip and I thought it would be cool to see some of the area attractions.  Ace the Himalaya provided a private shuttle and a very well educated and knowledgeable guide in Dil B Lama Tamang. Everything was new and exotic, I had hundreds of question and took hundreds of pictures. He was very patient, allowed me to take my time and absorb everything. I was allowed to tour at my pace and he was very knowledgeable. The Pashupati Temple is one of the most Sacred sites in the Hindu world. There here hundreds of Indians on pilgrimage. There were monkeys roaming the area and there were ongoing cremation ceremonies. The cremation services were very strange and foreign to me as a westerner. Witnessing these ceremonies and listening to his explanations, help me gain a real appreciation for their beliefs and see it not as a morbid display, but as a loving sendoff for your family member to the next life. I made this trip totally focused on my Everest experience, the Kathmandu Valley and World Heritage sites were not on my radar, but I can say that I thoroughly enjoyed the experience and I would recommend that you take the time to visit. COntact Ace the Himalaya, they are true professionals.",
