      {
        "review_id": 348565957,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r348565957-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Impressive cultural site",
        "text": "The complex is a must-see for everyone interested in Hindu culture. It is forbidden for non-Hindus to enter the main Shiva temple, and also foreigners have to pay an entrance fee of around 10 euros for the area around the Shiva temple, but that money is well spent. I was lucky enough to be there with my Nepali husband, who could explain to me the meaning of the rituals being performed all around, the goats running around freely, the dead bodies being prepared for cremation, the religious symbols and the hundreds of Shiva temples on the site. After fighting your way up a lifetime of steps, past the sadhus, beggars and fruit vendors, you can stretch your legs at a little street food stand, watch/feed the deer behind the stand and then enjoy a view of the Kathmandu valley. I definitely recommend this place to everyone interested in Hindu culture and heritage.",
        "review_tip": null,
